codex
The proposed sequence creates a pending PCC2 interrupt while MIEN is still clear, so the CPU line remains deasserted. That means the later `return` mutant preserves a low line and can pass the defect row. I also found that `session()` searches the entire accumulated transcript for its wait token; I’m checking how that affects waiting for a new breakpoint.
